  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 236 PM MDT MON AUG 31 2026\nThe pattern will remain active through the weekend as an upper\nlow spins over the Pacific Northwest. Moisture will continue to\nmove east through the area Thursday morning, with a 40-70%\nchance of showers in the Treasure Valley. Higher precipitation\nchances will prevail across southeast Oregon and the central \nIdaho mountains. A 10-30% chance of thunderstorms will develop \nin the afternoon and evening with daytime heating. Moderate \nprecipitation totals Wednesday night into Thursday are forecast \nin the mountains, with locally heavy amounts possible from \nthunderstorms. Precipitation chances will be minimal in the \nMagic Valley as the low stalls. Temperatures will cool another \nfew degrees to end up 10-15 degrees below normal. Winds will \nremain gusty across the area, especially higher terrain and near\nthe Nevada border.\n\nAdditional impulses will rotate around the main upper low\nstalled across the Pacific Northwest through the end of the \nperiod, bringing rounds of showers to the area, with \nthunderstorm potential each afternoon and evening. Temperatures\nare expected to remain below normal through the end of the \nperiod, although a gradual warming trend is forecast by the \nweekend into early next week. However, forecast confidence late \nin the period is low due to interaction between tropical\nactivity off the coast of Baja California and the upper low \nover the Pacific Northwest. There is potential for entrainment \nof tropical moisture across the West under southerly flow aloft,\nbut models vary considerably, so this potential will continue \nto be monitored.",
